{"name":"Lost in Time","hex":"#9fafbd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lost in time","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having happened or originated in a time so long ago that it has been completely forgotten or lost.","Lost during time travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lost_in_time"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lost in Time (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Lost in Time is a computer adventure game developed and published by Coktel Vision in 1993. It was promoted as being \"The first Interactive Adventure Film using Full Motion Video Technology\" and contained four graphical elements: full motion video, hand painted and digitized backgrounds and 3D decor."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/Lost_in_Time_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_in_Time_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q3259851"},{"title":"Lost in Time (2003 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lost in Time is a 2003 Hong Kong drama film directed by Derek Yee and starring Cecilia Cheung, Lau Ching-Wan and Louis Koo."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/03/LostInTime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_in_Time_(2003_film)","wikidata":"Q2132212"},{"title":"Lost in Time (Eric Benét album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lost in Time is the fifth studio album by American R&B recording artist Eric Benét, released November 30, 2010 on Reprise Records. It is the follow-up to Love & Life (2008). Production for the album took place during 2010 at various recording studios and was handled by Benét, George Nash, Jr., and Demonté Posey. Lost in Time contains musical elements of 1970s soul music and features guest appearances by Chrisette Michele, Faith Evans, Eddie Levert, Ledisi, and Benét's daughter, India."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/BenetLostinTime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_in_Time_(Eric_Ben%C3%A9t_album)","wikidata":"Q6684422"},{"title":"Time","blocks":[{"text":"Time is the continuous progression of existence that occurs in an apparently irreversible succession from the past, through the present, and into the future. Time dictates all forms of action, age, and causality, being a component quantity of various measurements used to sequence events, to compare the duration of events or the intervals between them, and to quantify rates of change of quantities in material reality or in conscious experience. Time is often referred to as the fourth dimension and the temporal dimension, in addition to the three spatial dimensions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/330px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time","wikidata":"Q11471"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The flow of sand in an hourglass can be used to measure the passage of one hour of time. It also concretely represents the present as being between the past and the future.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWooden_hourglass_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/500px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/1280px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/500px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Horizontal sundial in Canberra","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACanberra_(AU)%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg/330px-Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg/330px-Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"24-hour clock face in Florence","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlorence-Duomo-Clock.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg/500px-Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg/1280px-Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg/500px-Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A contemporary quartz watch, 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/ChipScaleClock2_HR.jpg/500px-ChipScaleClock2_HR.jpg?utm_source